---
source: crates/engram-cli/tests/cli/snapshot/help.rs
expression: "f.run_bare(& [\"harvest\", \"show\", \"--help\"])"
---
$ engramdb harvest show --help
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Print a budgeted digest of one session

Usage: engramdb harvest show [OPTIONS] <SESSION_ID>

Arguments:
  <SESSION_ID>
          Session id, or a unique prefix of one

Options:
      --max-chars <MAX_CHARS>
          Character budget for the digest. Defaults to `[harvest] digest_budget` (200000); `0` means unlimited

      --include-thinking
          Include the assistant's reasoning blocks (verbose)

      --include-sidechains
          Include subagent turns (verbose; subagents report back into the main thread, so their raw turns are largely duplicate volume)

      --no-tools
          Omit the tool-call trace, leaving prompts and prose only

      --all-projects
          Search every session on this machine, not just this project's

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-friendly colored output with formatting
          - json:   JSON output for programmatic parsing
          - plain:  Plain text output without colors

      --json
          Output as JSON

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

      --no-color
          No colored output

      --dir <DIR>
          Working directory (default: current directory)

      --embedding-backend <EMBEDDING_BACKEND>
          Embedding backend: auto, onnx, or ollama

      --in-process
          Force in-process model loading — never contact the shared embedding daemon. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_IN_PROCESS=1

      --spawn-daemon
          Spawn the shared embedding daemon if it is not already running, then route through it. By default the CLI only uses a daemon that is already running (connect-only)

      --no-maintenance
          Skip the automatic main-worktree maintenance pass (orphan-project cleanup + a quick store health check) for this invocation. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_DISABLE_AUTO_MAINTENANCE=1

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
--- stderr ---
